Article 20
(1) Advanced referral services as referred to in Article 18 letter b shall be established by the Regional Government to provide protection quickly and appropriately.
(2) Advanced referral services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be carried out by means including:
a. creating and implementing standard guidelines for excellent and women-friendly complaint or report handling;
b. integrating the complaint or report system between Regional Apparatus in the fields of communication, information, public services, villages, empowerment, women, security, legal aid and enforcement;
c. integrating the complaint or report system based on Sub-districts and Villages;
d. integrating the protection and legal assistance system with each designated legal aid organization;
e. opening complaint or report services based on digital media and digital applications; and
f. integrating the needs of victims for counseling, health services, visum et repertum and visum et psikiatrikum, as well as other service needs.
(3) Advanced referral services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided free of charge to victims in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 28
(1) Regional Government creates policies and programs that aim for Prevention against various acts of Discrimination, Violence, Exploitation, maltreatment, and/or neglect towards children.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1), are carried out by means of:
a. conducting socialization or counseling;
b. increasing awareness of the impact and legal consequences through program integration for families, communities, and the Business Sector;
c. internalization of anti-Violence, anti-Exploitation, anti-maltreatment, and anti-neglect values through formal education and non-formal education;
d. encouraging the establishment of children's forums as a platform for joint learning, support systems, and cadre development;
e. guidance and education for parents, guardians, or foster parents regarding parenting patterns in accordance with growth and development, appreciation, and outpouring of affection;
f. creating safe and child-friendly transportation; g. building and providing digital-based information systems and media that are easily accessible for information, protection requests, and reports; and
h. guidance towards the capacity of families, substitute families, or care institutions in caregiving abilities oriented towards growth and development and child appreciation.
(3) In implementing Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (2), Regional Government may involve and/or cooperate with media, communities, the Business Sector and/or educational institutions.

Article 29
(1) The Regional Government provides active and comprehensive protection to children from various actions: a. threats;
b. Violence;
c. Exploitation;
d. neglect;
e. Child Maltreatment; and
f. Injustice.
(2) Every form of threatening action as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a, whether verbal or nonverbal, that is intentionally directed at a child so as to make them feel threatened in life or safety is prohibited for any reason whatsoever.
(3) Every form of violent action as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, whether physical, psychological, or sexual violence that causes trauma to the child is prohibited for any reason whatsoever.
(4) Every form of exploitative action as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c that is carried out in any form and is not appropriate to the child's developmental age according to general views, legislation, or local wisdom and causes harm to the child is prohibited for any reason whatsoever.
(5) Every form of neglectful action as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d that disregards the responsibility as a parent, guardian, or foster parent toward the child is prohibited for any reason whatsoever.
(6) Every form of maltreatment action as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e that is carried out by exploiting closeness or abusing responsibility toward the child so as to cause physical or psychological trauma or is deemed contrary to laws and regulations is prohibited for any reason whatsoever.
(7) Every form of unjust action as referred to in paragraph (1) letter f, that is carried out by parents toward children that discriminates or shows favoritism as well as injustice in equality between males and females.

