Part Two
Duties and Responsibilities of Regional Government Article 11 (1) The duties and responsibilities of Regional Government as referred to in Article 10, include: a. making policies to encourage Prevention efforts against various forms of threats to women and children as well as providing comprehensive protection;
b. implementing policies with a victim-oriented approach;
c. conducting data collection and data verification related to information on women and children;
d. conducting various forms of cooperation to enhance protection efforts for women and children;
e. preparing supporting facilities and infrastructure; f. conducting guidance and empowerment for women;
g. providing safe houses for children that support development and growth as well as food intake and care; and
h. allocating budget according to needs and regional financial capacity;
i. actively involving Village Government, community and Business Sector in conducting protection efforts for women and children; and
j. realizing Purworejo Regency as a Women-Friendly and Child-Appropriate Regency.
(2) The duties and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Technical Regional Apparatus and may involve other related Regional Apparatus.
(3) The duties and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out with a victim-oriented approach based on laws and regulations.
